                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4fb30823-5e85-4df2-b4b5-2ed9abd34cd8",
                        "entry_id": "5e8d7d3e-b1d0-3b28-a621-e67b987d2e20",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "intercalated"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1bad8fb6-5b4f-3850-ad6a-03254ac80b18",
                        "entry_id": "5e8d7d3e-b1d0-3b28-a621-e67b987d2e20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To insert an extra leap day into a calendar in order to maintain synchrony with natural phenomena."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f714f6fd-a232-4eb7-8da4-4ce53262c0e6",
                                "sense_id": "1bad8fb6-5b4f-3850-ad6a-03254ac80b18",
                                "text": "'[T]is wonderful where or when we ever got anything of this which we call wisdom, poetry, virtue. We never got it on any dated calendar day. Some heavenly days must have been intercalated somewhere."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9222a4ad-0956-48b4-b5d9-f30cec4256b7",
                                "sense_id": "1bad8fb6-5b4f-3850-ad6a-03254ac80b18",
                                "text": "At some unknown period, the five days, known to the present time by the names of the five Gathic hymns of Zarathushtra, were intercalated at the end of the twelfth month, to complete the three hundred and sixty-five days of the solar year."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b10ac026-bfd1-3135-b8ee-b43d0b99092f",
                        "entry_id": "5e8d7d3e-b1d0-3b28-a621-e67b987d2e20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To insert an extra month into a calendar for the same purpose, such as for the Hebrew calendar."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8765cedb-2c26-4f2c-a633-9050c256bf3c",
                                "sense_id": "b10ac026-bfd1-3135-b8ee-b43d0b99092f",
                                "text": "The Sages once overheard three shepherds discussing what weather is characteristic of Adar, and if that weather does not occur, it is not really Adar. As a result, the Sages intercalated the year and added Adar II."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4fa59f86-2ee1-3179-83ae-63069ebd9b12",
                        "entry_id": "5e8d7d3e-b1d0-3b28-a621-e67b987d2e20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To insert a substance between two or more molecules, bases, cells, or tissues."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a72ae28-b2b0-3762-a963-99d21fad6de9",
                        "entry_id": "5e8d7d3e-b1d0-3b28-a621-e67b987d2e20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To insert anything somewhere (especially between other things), such as an affix into a word. (Compare interpolate.)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c105818f-e306-4a8f-a065-cf49e861afaf",
                                "sense_id": "3a72ae28-b2b0-3762-a963-99d21fad6de9",
                                "text": "... the personal pronouns which form the terminations of the verb, or by an intercalated suffix, the nature and relation of its objects and its subject , and to distinguish whether the object be animate or inanimate, ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9da7b3ee-bf84-4a95-bdd2-6f0a05d4dd78",
                                "sense_id": "3a72ae28-b2b0-3762-a963-99d21fad6de9",
                                "text": "Sometimes f or s is intercalated to lighten the pronunciation : kommen, Kunft ; können, Kunst ; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73a19298-5d12-4746-9710-596cdbdbbb27",
                                "sense_id": "3a72ae28-b2b0-3762-a963-99d21fad6de9",
                                "text": "-erole ← -er- (< -ÅR) + -ole ( < -EOLU): maierole. A lengthened var. of -ole, this suffix appears in the late Middle Ages, formed through “false division”, namely the secondary rapprochement of, say, bannerole (banniere + -ole) or casserole with ban- or cass-. Is the -er- […] intercalated for rhythmic of differentiatory purposes? This \"interfix\" conveys no semantic message: It simply serves as an occasionally handy grammatical tool."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7a9960c-12d1-4d80-a88e-b65f9df764da",
                                "sense_id": "3a72ae28-b2b0-3762-a963-99d21fad6de9",
                                "text": "... they were interpreted and modified in the light of Pythagorean harmonies and other mystical manipulations of vowels and letters. The intercalated letters are intended to be the first ten letters of the alphabet as in line 602ff."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d32f9030-d497-4736-ab8b-eff799963475",
                                "sense_id": "3a72ae28-b2b0-3762-a963-99d21fad6de9",
                                "text": "Description: Color translucent white; shell cap shaped; sculpture of approximately 40 radiating ribs with intercalated threads alternating between ribs; concentric ribs intersecting radial ribs; anal fasciole relatively short, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "82696e80-ba0f-497f-b8e3-ea1ea4dbad85",
                        "source_entry_id": "5e8d7d3e-b1d0-3b28-a621-e67b987d2e20",
                        "source_sense_description": "insert an extra day into a calendar",
                        "target_lang_word": "intercaler",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "intercaler",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b2979b5-79c6-3b03-9d38-a8b162cd6895",
                                        "entry_id": "09084f35-0dd2-3bcc-8a82-aef46c2e0550",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Insérer un jour, de quatre ans en quatre ans, dans le mois de février, afin de caler plus exactement l'année avec le cours du soleil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d041e00b-3612-4f24-8506-9a4a4c765c17",
                                                "sense_id": "9b2979b5-79c6-3b03-9d38-a8b162cd6895",
                                                "text": "Dans les années bissextiles on intercale un jour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6d03559-4830-36bd-bc6d-bc0c4c2a4c01",
                                        "entry_id": "09084f35-0dd2-3bcc-8a82-aef46c2e0550",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ajouter quelque chose après coup."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90f72338-1abc-4751-8054-cf343364ed42",
                                                "sense_id": "a6d03559-4830-36bd-bc6d-bc0c4c2a4c01",
                                                "text": "Au lieu de nettoyer les graines ébossées, G. Duval a imaginé d'agir sur la bourre en intercalant entre l’ébourreur et l’ébosseur un crible tronconique dont la surface latérale est garnie de feuilles de zinc perforées […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80cb6b04-f701-4797-8ba0-d62b3a36bb90",
                                                "sense_id": "a6d03559-4830-36bd-bc6d-bc0c4c2a4c01",
                                                "text": "Sur la route, ce furent les premières chaussées modernes construites par Trésauguet, en France, et par Mac-Adam, en Angleterre vers 1760, qui firent rechercher des procédés un peu moins primitifs que le sabot qu'on intercalait entre la roue et le sol, la chaîne d'enrayage et le rondin qui embarraient la jante près d'un rai."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "556f6560-2a10-4f39-b847-9b3f9e4a6e56",
                                                "sense_id": "a6d03559-4830-36bd-bc6d-bc0c4c2a4c01",
                                                "text": "Intercaler un mot, une ligne dans un acte, un article dans un compte, un passage dans un texte."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
